 "method_notes": "H&F Starting School 2026 brochure (common definitions / community schools policy, p.28-30) and community schools determined arrangements 2026/27: unless a school's own criteria say otherwise, distance is a straight line ('as the crow flies') from the child's home 'address point' (Ordnance Survey data) to the main entrance gate for pupils (community policy: nearest entrance for pupils), measured by H&F Council's computerised measuring system; nearest child gets highest priority. Shared address points (flats) are separated by random allocation/draw. The council's hints-and-tips leaflet states 'Distance is determined in straight line for all applications'. Community oversubscription order: looked after, exceptional need, siblings, children of staff, distance. Faith and free schools use foundation/open, nursery, Pupil Premium or multi-site categories (see school notes). Figures are in miles ('x of a mile').",
 "method_source": "https://www.lbhf.gov.uk/sites/default/files/2025-03/community-schools-determined-arrangements-2026-27.pdf",
