 "gaps": "2026 figures come from the council's Starting school 2027 brochure, via a copy on St Peter's C of E Primary's website (lbhf.gov.uk itself refuses automated requests). Faith schools whose last place went under a faith-only criterion are recorded as no_distance_offers (Good Shepherd, Holy Cross, Larmenier & Sacred Heart, and 2025/2024 rows for these that were earlier recorded as distances); St John's Walham Green 2026 open places all went to siblings. Good Shepherd's '2d' does not exist in its 2027 criteria (2a-2c are sub-priorities of criterion 2, baptised Catholics); treated as criterion 2. Holy Cross 2024 'criterion 10' is not in the summarised 2027 criteria and is left as a distance. New King's Road School (formerly Thomas's Academy) prints exactly the same 2026 figures as its 2025 ones (0.400 miles, nursery 0.959), possibly copied forward. 2025 and 2024 figures come from Wayback Machine copies of the council brochures (2026-entry and 2025-entry), read from per-school 'How places were offered' boxes in a two-column layout. Postcodes, types and PANs from the 2026-entry brochure (not GIAS-checked); Miles Coverdale 'W12 8J J' and Fulham Bilingual 'SW6 3A A' normalised; Earl's Court Free School Primary and West London Free School Primary both print W6 0LB. For schools with separate foundation/open or two-site cut-offs (St Peter's, St John's Walham Green, All Saints, Earl's Court, Nishkam-style splits) one value is recorded and the others are in criterion_note. Individual academy/faith measuring points not checked beyond the brochure; straight line assumed. The London Oratory School Junior House (in the 2025 brochure only, PAN 20, no breakdown) excluded as it admits at age 7, not Reception.",
